          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Goneril\",\"addressee\":\"Lear\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Sir, I love you more than word can wield the matter;\\nDearer than eyesight, space, and liberty;\\nBeyond what can be valu’d, rich or rare;\\nNo less than life, with grace, health, beauty, honour;\\nAs much as child e’er lov’d, or father found;\\nA love that makes breath poor and speech unable;\\nBeyond all manner of so much I love you.\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"Goneril directly presents her love for Lear as a true emotional state. The surrounding hyperbolic comparisons intensify that avowal, regardless of whether it is sincere.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"I love you more than word can wield the matter;\\nDearer than eyesight, space, and liberty;\\nBeyond what can be valu’d, rich or rare;\\nNo less than life, with grace, health, beauty, honour;\\nAs much as child e’er lov’d, or father found;\\nA love that makes breath poor and speech unable;\\nBeyond all manner of so much I love you.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.96,\"reason\":\"The focal expression avows a present state but does not commit Goneril to future conduct, continued loyalty, obedience, care, or another specified obligation. Lear’s subsequent grant is his own act and must not be transferred onto her expression as undertaking force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"We make thee lady: to thine and Albany’s issue\\nBe this perpetual.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"This is a formally solicited, rhetorically developed answer in a public proceeding, not a reflex-like affective outburst. Its emotional language remains organized as an avowal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Goneril,\\nOur eldest born, speak first.\\n\\nGONERIL.\\nSir, I love you more than word can wield the matter;\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.84,\"reason\":\"Beyond avowing love, the expression functions moderately as competitive praise and self-presentation in Lear’s announced love test, where professing the greatest love is tied to receiving the largest bounty. This strategic function is contextually salient but does not displace the expression’s dominant avowal force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Which of you shall we say doth love us most?\\nThat we our largest bounty may extend\\nWhere nature doth with merit challenge.—Goneril,\\nOur eldest born, speak first.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Sir, I love you more than word can wield the matter;\\nDearer than eyesight, space, and liberty;\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"In a public court proceeding, Lear asks his daughters to declare which loves him most and explicitly links the declarations to the distribution of his kingdom. Goneril, called on first, delivers the focal avowal as the opening of an extended, superlative profession of filial love. Lear responds by granting her and Albany a large hereditary portion.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"mixed\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"Goneril undertakes no specified commitment in the focal expression or its surrounding profession; she asserts and magnifies her love. Lear gives the declaration favorable practical uptake by immediately awarding territory, but that reward does not convert her avowal into a promise. The later supplied evidence that Lear’s elder daughters wronged and harmed him weighs against sincerity or enduring affection, without changing the original utterance’s avowal form or conclusively revealing Goneril’s inner state at that moment.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied passages are recognisable as William Shakespeare’s King Lear, specifically the opening love test and later scenes involving Lear and Cordelia.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence clearly establishes the public, reward-linked setting and later conduct inconsistent with the profession. It does not directly disclose Goneril’s private mental state at the moment of speaking, so the sincerity and exact degree of actual affection remain uncertain.\"}"
        }
